WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.050
Two baby boys: one born
in Hart, in Hampshire,

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.470
one in Blackpool.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.890
The boy in Hart can expect
to live ten years longer.

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:15.330
In 2022 to 2024, the ten local areas
with the highest life expectancy were all

5
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.870
in the south of England.

6
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.250
The ten lowest were concentrated in
the north of England and Scotland.

7
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.330
So why should where you're born
decide how long you're likely to live?

8
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.130
In this mission, you'll map a divide
that runs across the whole country,

9
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.990
region by region.

10
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.510
Then you'll sort its causes into economic,

11
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.510
political and social.

12
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.750
Your mission: explain why a boy in Hart
can expect to outlive one in Blackpool.
